# Region Management

The Choreo CLI supports multiple deployment regions (US and EU). Region management is handled by two main files:

1. [internal/region/config.go](mdc:internal/region/config.go) - Core region configuration and management
   - Defines available regions (US, EU)
   - Manages current region selection
   - Provides region-specific configurations
   - Thread-safe region operations

2. [internal/region/store.go](mdc:internal/region/store.go) - Region persistence
   - Persists region selection using system keyring
   - Uses same storage mechanism as other CLI stores
   - Provides region storage operations (get, set, remove)

## Key Features

- Default region is US if no region is stored
- Region selection persists across CLI sessions
- Thread-safe operations using mutex locks
- Environment-specific configurations (dev, stage, prod)
- Consistent with other CLI storage patterns

## Related Files

The region functionality integrates with the auth system:
- [internal/auth/auth.go](mdc:internal/auth/auth.go) - Uses region info for authentication
- [internal/auth/token-store.go](mdc:internal/auth/token-store.go) - Region-specific token storage
